notes:
Entered Jul 2010.   Bordeaux 2 University. Number of specimens in the herbarium unknown.  Bound volumes in the herbarium include:
H. De Rochebrune: Herbier de De Rochebrune 53 boxes (1850-1860);
Jean-François Laterrade (1784-1858), Flore de la Gironde 7 boxes;
Jean-François Laterrade, Flore générale 8 boxes;
Lucien Dupray (-1902), Antoine Mougeot (1815-1889) and Casimir Roumeguère (1828-1892) Algues de France 10 parts;
Casimir Roumeguère Lichens d'Europe 39 parts;
Casimir Roumeguère Mousses de l'Aude 11 parts;
Casimir Roumeguère Mousses Alp. d'Europe 22 parts;
Pierre Tranquille Husnot (1840-1929) Algae Europae 11 parts.

Updated Nov 2009.
Updated 24 March 2021
CLP  means College, Laguna,  Philippines; it houses around 2600 herbarium specimens and 11,000 local and foreign wood samples; digitization (QR coding),  including inventory and  relabeling of wood samples is  on going (started during the 2nd semester or 2019);
